WEBVTT

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.020
﻿Player Tatsuya Yuuki has declined
﻿to enter match four of the quarterfinals.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.790
﻿- He bowed out of the battle?
- ﻿Player Susumu Sazaki

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.860
﻿- What's going on, Sei!?
- ﻿is winner by default.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.430
﻿Don't ask me.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.130
﻿Why on earth...

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.700
﻿Why!?

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.970
﻿Yuuki, why!?

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.680
Please tell me why you're
﻿bowing out of the regional—

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.550
﻿Hey, Iori.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.650
﻿Gonda.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.580
﻿President Yuuki's not here.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.750
﻿Tatsuya Yuuki isn't here as captain
﻿of the model-building club, either.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.890
﻿What do you mean?

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:51.560
﻿The president has...

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.960
﻿He's taken an indefinite
﻿leave from school.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.800
﻿Okay, okay.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.230
﻿So, Tatsuya Yuuki quit Gunpla Battle,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.570
﻿and then he quit that school thing.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:41.240
﻿I asked why he left school,
﻿but nobody knows.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.710
﻿Even the teachers just heard
﻿it was for personal reasons.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.740
﻿He turned tail and ran.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.250
﻿He was afraid to face our Gunpla.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:53.520
﻿I can't believe I wanted to
﻿fight such a loser.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.090
﻿I feel stupid.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.390
﻿Stop it, Reiji.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.820
﻿Well, but...

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.660
﻿Thanks to that, we're a step closer
﻿to winning the tournament, right?

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.260
Reiji!

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.660
﻿Yuuki isn't like that.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.100
﻿He chickened out!

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.000
﻿He gave up honor and pride
﻿and ran away from us!

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:21.580
Sei.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:23.850
﻿Don't ever talk about him again.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.550
﻿Our next game is the semifinals.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:28.750
﻿Let's win it, Sei.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.020
﻿Y-Yeah.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:45.340
﻿We will now begin match one
﻿of the semifinals...

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.510
﻿in the regional qualifying tournament.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:53.140
﻿Winning that game by default
﻿must've brought me luck.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.460
﻿I've enhanced the weapons
of my Gyan Gya Gyan even more.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:09.090
﻿With it, I'll get my ticket
to enter the World Tournament!

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:17.800
﻿Ahead!

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.080
﻿- Reiji!
- ﻿How could you...!

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.090
﻿Gotcha!

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.130
﻿You're not...!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:49.730
﻿Not at all...

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.100
﻿A worthy opponent!

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.970
﻿Gyan Gya Gyan!

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.410
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.020
﻿Darn it.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:10.390
﻿Next time, my Gyan will...

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.190
﻿My bad, Sei.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:16.290
﻿I thought it'd be
﻿an easy win...

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:18.760
﻿So I let my guard down.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:19.960
﻿Reiji.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.770
- ﻿In this battle—
- ﻿I'm starving all of a sudden.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.370
﻿Sorry, but I'm going home.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:32.480
﻿It's good that they were able
﻿to advance to the final round,

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.280
﻿but Reiji's maneuvering seemed to be off.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.520
﻿At this rate, I'm not sure
﻿if they'll win the upcoming final.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:44.260
﻿Maybe he's still bothered
﻿that President Yuuki withdrew.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.360
﻿Even so, he must get past it.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.530
﻿Reiji should know it, too.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:56.970
﻿That someone who has
﻿no reason to battle cannot win.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.030
<i>﻿Trial battle ended.</i>

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.870
﻿Your time was 30 seconds.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.540
﻿Your accuracy was 98%.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:40.340
﻿You have the best scores
﻿of all the fighter cadets here.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.110
﻿Tatsuya.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:48.650
﻿﻿And you did it with your own Gunpla
not a PPSE Works model.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.520
﻿They'll have to choose you
﻿at the tomorrow's ceremony,

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:55.530
﻿and you'll succeed to
﻿the name as third-generation.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:00.700
﻿Where to?

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:03.970
﻿Don't worry.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.770
﻿I'll be back by tomorrow's ceremony.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:10.170
﻿Do as you wish.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.910
﻿No matter what you do,

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.450
﻿this fate was one you wanted, too.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:39.700
﻿If we'd fought against
﻿Yuuki's Zaku in the semifinals,

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.410
﻿then probably...

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:48.050
﻿No matter what he said,
﻿I'm sure Reiji felt the same way.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:52.950
﻿But neither of us thought
﻿we'd run away from the battle.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.890
﻿But then, why did Yuuki...?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:05.300
﻿I want you to perfect it
﻿before the championship.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:09.200
﻿I want to fight against
﻿your truly completed Gunpla.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:13.900
﻿And the championship is
﻿the perfect stage for that.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:19.680
﻿Ours is still stronger.
﻿We'll prove it in this tournament!

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.910
﻿I'm looking forward to it.

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:32.220
﻿I came all the way to this world.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:36.260
﻿What on earth am I doing?

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:42.200
﻿Sei, Miss Kousaka is here to see you.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.100
﻿Okay.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:48.010
﻿I'm sorry for calling suddenly.

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:50.670
﻿There's no need to apologize.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.580
﻿You want to use our compressor, right?

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.210
﻿Yeah.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.380
﻿Do you know how?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:57.210
﻿I know it from the art club.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.380
﻿Okay, off we go.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:00.220
﻿Yeah!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.030
﻿You're pretty good, Kousaka.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:11.830
﻿You think?

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:15.130
﻿Isn't Reiji here today?

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.840
﻿Actually, I haven't seen him
﻿since last week's semifinals.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.740
﻿He must be still bothered
﻿about President Yuuki.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.580
﻿Probably.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.550
﻿He can't hide his feelings,
﻿so it's pretty obvious.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:29.380
﻿Yeah.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.890
﻿I was the one who asked Reiji
﻿to play Gunpla Battle.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:37.650
﻿He seemed uninterested.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:43.760
﻿But I wanted him to
﻿control my Build Strike so badly.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:49.630
﻿There was one time when
﻿Reiji came late to the tournament.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:53.170
﻿I thought, if he isn't
﻿interested in Gunpla,

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:55.510
﻿it's only natural
﻿he wouldn't show up.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.110
﻿As much as it ticked me off.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.210
﻿But he came.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.210
﻿Later I heard from Mr. Ral...

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.780
﻿that he was with Mr. Ral's friends,
﻿training hard for Gunpla Battle.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:06.720
﻿I see.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:12.820
﻿He went through all that because
﻿he wanted to fight Yuuki.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.060
﻿Now that Yuuki's gone, I can understand
﻿him losing his motivation.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.230
﻿Will he quit Gunpla Battle altogether?

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.960
﻿No, never.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.970
﻿Maybe I just want to believe it,

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.400
﻿but I think for Reiji, Gunpla is...

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.580
﻿I'm envious.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.280
﻿About what?

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.650
﻿By the way...

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:40.720
﻿What are you staring at, mom!?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.590
﻿Please don't mind me.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:45.390
﻿That's impossible!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.400
﻿Go, GN-X!

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.570
﻿Don't lose, Asshimar!

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.010
﻿Take this!

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:10.980
﻿Oh, Reiji.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:14.220
﻿Are you looking for
﻿someone to battle with?

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:17.350
﻿No. Who'd play with such kids?

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.920
﻿You're right.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.390
﻿You only started playing
﻿Gunpla Battle two months ago.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:26.230
﻿But you're now a finalist in
﻿the qualifying tournament.

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:29.330
﻿It's not too much to say
﻿your ability is world-level.

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.000
﻿Thanks.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:36.270
﻿When you really look at it,
﻿don't you think it's silly?

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.570
﻿What is?

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:42.650
﻿Everybody is so serious
﻿about playing with toys.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:44.650
﻿Don't you like it?

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:46.680
﻿I just don't get it.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.990
﻿You can quit if you like.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.920
﻿Building and battling Gunpla
﻿is merely a hobby.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:59.030
Unlike the Mobile Suit Gundam story,
﻿we're not in a state of war,

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.870
﻿and we don't have to
﻿put our lives on the line.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:05.500
﻿It's just played for pleasure.
﻿You're absolutely right.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.610
﻿But... No, for that very reason...

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:13.380
﻿people can be enthralled by
﻿Gunpla and Gunpla Battle.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.010
﻿Because they like it,
﻿they can take it seriously.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:21.220
﻿I can see seriousness in you.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.990
﻿Like that guy over there.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.740
﻿Reiji! What's the hurry?

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.350
﻿Sei, lend me your Gunpla!

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:50.150
﻿What's wrong?

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:56.420
﻿While the final round is coming right up,
﻿I might damage it or even break it.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:58.060
﻿But let me borrow it.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:00.390
﻿Please!

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:01.960
﻿I already told you.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.130
﻿This Gunpla,

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:07.530
﻿the Build Strike, is made just for you.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:10.700
Sei.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.540
﻿But I'm coming along.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:17.440
﻿He's waiting, right?

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.290
﻿Reiji, why are we at school?

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:35.790
﻿Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:38.630
﻿President Yuuki, why?

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:44.230
﻿Please tell us why you bowed out.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:45.900
﻿Why you left school...

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.740
﻿Never mind his reasons.

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:52.610
﻿He's standing here now
﻿with his Gunpla in his hands.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:54.140
That's all we need.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.880
﻿Yeah, we'll find out his reason
﻿through this battle.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:03.590
<i>﻿Please set your GP Base.</i>

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:09.530
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.330
<i>﻿Field 1, Space.</i>

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.780
<i>﻿Please set your Gunpla.</i>

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:34.480
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.120
﻿Build Strike Gundam!

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:37.290
﻿Let's go!

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.930
﻿Zaku Amazing, Tatsuya Yuuki.
﻿Here I come!

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.920
﻿I sense it. I can sense...

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:44.590
﻿I sense their feelings.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.660
﻿I thought you chickened out.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:48.930
﻿Sorry.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:50.660
﻿I had reasons I can't share.

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:53.760
﻿It doesn't matter

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.700
﻿All I wanted to do is fight with you!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:15:59.600
﻿Same here!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.110
﻿Old man Ral told me,

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.480
﻿Gunpla is just played for pleasure.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:13.580
﻿That's why people take it seriously!

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:16.150
﻿That's how it is for me.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.290
﻿And now you, too.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:27.630
﻿Reiji, I'll fix it no matter
﻿how many times it breaks!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.000
﻿Go forward!

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.810
﻿I'll show you my seriousness!

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:40.940
﻿I'll respond to it
﻿with my raging spirit!

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.620
﻿Reiji. Yuuki.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:55.260
﻿I can hardly sit still, Mr. Ral.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.090
﻿Fellini.

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:01.530
﻿Seeing a battle like this
﻿gets me all fired up.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.310
﻿It's not over yet!

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:31.260
﻿Tatsuya, I finally understand
﻿why you're so obsessed with them.

00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:35.270
﻿Takeshi Iori's son, Sei Iori.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:40.040
﻿And Reiji, a boy with control skills
﻿that are equal to yours.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:44.170
﻿If you're a man, you would
﻿want to fight with them.

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:45.940
﻿If you're a fighter!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.680
﻿Not just yet!

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:30.890
﻿Not yet.

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.260
﻿Yeah, not yet!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.840
﻿This is our...!

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:51.910
﻿This is my...!

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:57.080
﻿- Gunpla!

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:09.190
﻿You're amazing.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:13.360
﻿And I was truly convinced.

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:15.470
﻿Tatsuya Yuuki,

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:19.070
﻿you're worthy of assuming
﻿the name as third generation.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:23.170
﻿I'm not thrilled with
﻿the victory at hand.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:25.180
﻿What I'm aiming for, no,

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.610
﻿what we're aiming for is

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:30.480
﻿much further away.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:37.850
﻿We'll meet again, Iori and Reiji.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:42.290
﻿No, we'll definitely meet again.
﻿In the near future.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.960
﻿We lost completely.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:48.430
﻿So completely that
﻿there's no room for excuses.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:51.270
﻿Yuuki was really great.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:53.480
But...

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.570
﻿We'll win next time.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:57.740
﻿Yeah!

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:01.780
﻿Seeing the Gundam X Maoh
﻿that Mao built,

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:05.480
﻿and battling with
﻿Yuuki's Zaku Amazing,

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:09.190
﻿I'm filled with ideas.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.360
﻿But after that battle,
﻿the Build Strike is...

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:19.130
﻿True, it'll be hard to fix it
﻿in time for the final round.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:24.000
﻿But do you think I just sat by
﻿while you were gone?

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:26.340
﻿Sei, you mean...?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.370
﻿We don't have just one Gunpla!

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:36.380
﻿This is...

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:38.150
﻿the Build Gundam Mk-II.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:41.250
﻿Model number RX-178B.

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.990
﻿It was developed by the Titans,
﻿an elite special unit...

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:48.060
﻿of the Earth Federation Forces
﻿created to hunt down Zeon remnants.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:49.390
﻿In the anime setting,

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.330
﻿its armor and frame used
﻿older standard parts.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:53.760
﻿But mine is different.

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:57.270
﻿Look here!
﻿I used the newest materials.

00:20:57.670 --> 00:21:00.970
﻿I hardly get it, but...

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:03.140
﻿With this, we can fight!

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:05.580
﻿With the Gunpla you built!

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:06.980
﻿Yeah!

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:10.450
﻿Let's nail the final round!

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.880
﻿Sure!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:23.390
We will now begin the final round of
﻿the regional qualifying tournament.

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:24.860
﻿Let's go!

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:26.430
﻿Yeah, man.

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:33.070
﻿Our opponent is Mr. Kato,
﻿a regular tournament veteran.

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.910
﻿Who's that? Never heard of him.

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:37.010
﻿I knew you'd say that.

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:42.980
﻿If we win this, we're going
﻿to the World Tournament.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.920
﻿And there, even more
﻿amazing players are waiting!

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:54.460
﻿- Build Gundam Mk-II!
- ﻿Let's go!

00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:36.290
﻿I can't believe it.

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:39.260
﻿Tatsuya Yuuki bowed out?

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:41.730
﻿Watch carefully.

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:44.470
﻿You may fight with one of these two.

00:23:44.470 --> 00:23:46.400
﻿The white Gunpla is going to win.

00:23:55.920 --> 00:23:58.090
﻿Okay, everyone.
﻿It's time for the goodies.

00:23:58.090 --> 00:24:00.290
﻿Beaches and swimsuits!

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:02.290
Next episode, "World-Level Ability".

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:04.290
Gunpla Battle! Ready! Go!
